  "preregistration": {
    "frozen": "2026-08-25",
    "question": "Does Hillel M4 (neutral NMe2/NO2 push-pull azobenzene) still show an S0/T1 crossing near 110\u00b0 when recomputed with Hillel 2024's own method, SF-TDDFT in ORCA?",
    "hypothesis": "M4 still shows a both-converged S0/T1 crossing near 110\u00b0 when S0 and T1 are taken from the SF-TDDFT manifold at Hillel 2024\u2019s electronic-structure level.",
    "crossing_definition_quoted": "\u0394E(\u03c6) = E(T1, \u03c6) \u2212 E(S0, \u03c6), both SF-TDDFT total energies (E_SCF + E_root) after constrained CNNC opts of the spin-assigned roots. S0 = lowest SF root with \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9 \u2248 0; T1 = lowest SF root with \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9 \u2248 2. A crossing is a sign change of \u0394E on neighboring both-converged, both-spin-assigned points, plus that pair\u2019s linear interpolant. \u201cNear 110\u00b0\u201d means the interpolant is in 90\u2013135\u00b0, or the pair is 120\u00b0/105\u00b0. Unconverged or spin-contaminated neighbors are not a bracket.",
    "falsifiers_quoted": {
      "1": "No both-converged, spin-assigned sign change of \u0394E in 90\u2013135\u00b0 \u2192 hypothesis not supported. \u201cIt did not reproduce for us under these conditions.\u201d",
      "2": "Sign change exists, interpolant outside 90\u2013135\u00b0 \u2192 the \u201cnear 110\u00b0\u201d claim is not supported.",
      "3": "Fewer than one neighboring both-converged, spin-assigned pair in 90\u2013135\u00b0 \u2192 inconclusive. \u201cThe SF-TDDFT grid did not decide.\u201d"
    }
