  "iroot_notes": "Assignment is by \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9, not filename or IROOT index (PLAN/PREREG). S0 = lowest SF root with \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9\u22480 (Mult 1); T1 = lowest with \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9\u22482 (Mult 3). A root with \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9\u22481 is contaminated and is not used. At 105/120/135, IROOT 1 is the singlet and IROOT 2 the triplet (tutorial default), on both S0-opt and T1-opt final geometries. At 90\u00b0, the order is swapped on the diagnostic SPs (IROOT 1 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=2.314693 Mult 3; IROOT 2 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=0.280977 Mult 1) and remains swapped on both converged opts (S0-opt last: IROOT 1 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=2.250431 Mult 3, IROOT 2 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=0.306315 Mult 1; T1-opt last: IROOT 1 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=2.266676 Mult 3, IROOT 2 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=0.257362 Mult 1). The 90\u00b0 opt inputs were rewritten after the SPs (m4_s0_phi_090 IROOT 1\u21922; m4_t1_phi_090 IROOT 2\u21921) and FOLLOWIROOT stayed on that assignment through convergence. Residual SF contamination: assigned S0 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=0.140925\u20130.306315; assigned T1 \u27e8S\u00b2\u27e9=2.192470\u20132.293241. None near 1. SP energies were used only to confirm this assignment and are not in the claim table.",
